Write the `closing` slot.

Intent: two sentences restating factually what the period cost and what it produced. This is the
last thing in the document.

If your allowlist includes the `late-period.*` facts, add ONE more sentence stating how much of the
work landed in the window's final days, as the measurement it is: "the final
{{fact:late-period.days}} days carried ...". Do not characterize it as momentum, a ramp, a slowdown,
a trend, an indication of what is in flight, or a signal about what comes next. If those facts are
not on your allowlist the window was too short to measure a tail: write nothing about it, and do not
mention that it is missing.

No justification of the spend, no trajectory verdict, no ROI language, no predictions, and no
statement or implication of a reporting cadence.
